.TH SIMRV-BENCHMARK 1 "November 2026" "SimRV 3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
simrv-benchmark \- run and compare native SimRV benchmarks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B simrv-benchmark
.RI [ options ]
.I elf-file | suite-name
.br
.B simrv-benchmark compare
.I baseline.json candidate.json
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B simrv-benchmark
runs guest workloads with SimRV, optionally compares results with Spike, and
exports measurements as JSON. Comparison mode computes speedup from two saved
benchmark results.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-runs \fIN\fR, \-\-warmup \fIN\fR
Set measured and warmup run counts.
.TP
.B \-\-mode \fIMODE\fR, \-\-ca
Select \fBfast\fR, \fBdetailed\fR, or \fBcycle-accurate\fR execution. \fB--ca\fR
selects cycle-accurate mode.
.TP
.B \-\-nanobench
Run in-process microbenchmarks.
.TP
.B \-\-spike [\fIPATH\fR]
Compare against Spike, using the supplied executable or automatic discovery.
.TP
.B \-\-suite \fINAME\fR
Run a standard benchmark suite.
.TP
.B \-e, \-\-limit \fIN\fR
Set the instruction execution limit.
.TP
.B \-\-isa \fIISA\fR, \-\-vlen \fIBITS\fR
Override the guest ISA or vector register length.
.TP
.B \-\-json \fIPATH\fR
Write benchmark measurements as JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-timeout \fISECONDS\fR
Set the execution timeout.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR simrv (1)
